    createStaticVNode('<h1 id="_17-fan-module" tabindex="-1">17. Fan Module <a class="header-anchor" href="#_17-fan-module" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;17. Fan Module&quot;">​</a></h1><h2 id="_17-1-introduction" tabindex="-1">17.1 Introduction <a class="header-anchor" href="#_17-1-introduction" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;17.1 Introduction&quot;">​</a></h2><p>This section introduces the fan module, a compact cooling component with built-in motor drive circuitry and adjustable speed control. Pairing the fan module with an environmental sensor, such as a temperature and humidity sensor, enables the creation of a smart fan system that adjusts its speed automatically based on ambient temperature.</p><img loading="lazy" height="433" width="554" src="' + _imports_0 + '" class="common_img" style="width:300px;"><h2 id="_17-2-technical-specifications" tabindex="-1">17.2 Technical Specifications <a class="header-anchor" href="#_17-2-technical-specifications" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;17.2 Technical Specifications&quot;">​</a></h2><table tabindex="0"><thead><tr><th style="text-align:center;">Parameter</th><th style="text-align:center;">Description</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td style="text-align:center;">Operating voltage</td><td style="text-align:center;">5 V</td></tr><tr><td style="text-align:center;">Connector model</td><td style="text-align:center;">5264-4AW</td></tr><tr><td style="text-align:center;">Mounting compatibility</td><td style="text-align:center;">LEGO-compatible hole spacing</td></tr><tr><td style="text-align:center;">Dimensions</td><td style="text-align:center;">34.1 × 21.0 × 14.4 mm</td></tr></tbody></table><h2 id="_17-3-hands-on-project" tabindex="-1">17.3 Hands-On Project <a class="header-anchor" href="#_17-3-hands-on-project" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;17.3 Hands-On Project&quot;">​</a></h2><h3 id="_17-3-1-project-introduction" tabindex="-1">17.3.1 Project Introduction <a class="header-anchor" href="#_17-3-1-project-introduction" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;17.3.1 Project Introduction&quot;">​</a></h3><p>This project uses the programmable buttons on the controller to regulate fan speed. Short-pressing the left button increases the fan speed, while short-pressing the right button decreases it, limiting the speed to a range between 0 and 100. This project introduces variable storage and conditional logic to achieve smooth, variable speed control.</p><h3 id="_17-3-2-hardware-wiring" tabindex="-1">17.3.2 Hardware Wiring <a class="header-anchor" href="#_17-3-2-hardware-wiring" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;17.3.2 Hardware Wiring&quot;">​</a></h3><ul><li>Connect the fan module to port <strong>A</strong> of the controller using a 4-pin module cable.</li></ul><img loading="lazy" height="421" width="1040" src="' + _imports_1 + '" class="common_img" style="width:500px;"><div class="note custom-block github-alert"><p class="custom-block-title">NOTE</p><p></p><p><strong>This module supports connection to any port among A, B, C, or D on the controller. Ensure that the port selected in the program matches the physical wiring.</strong></p></div><h3 id="_17-3-3-adding-extensions" tabindex="-1">17.3.3 Adding Extensions <a class="header-anchor" href="#_17-3-3-adding-extensions" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;17.3.3 Adding Extensions&quot;">​</a></h3><ul><li>Select <strong>Fan module</strong> under the <strong>Output module</strong> category.</li></ul><img loading="lazy" height="1040" width="1920" src="' + _imports_2 + '" class="common_img" style="width:800px;"><h3 id="_17-3-4-complete-program-and-analysis" tabindex="-1">17.3.4 Complete Program and Analysis <a class="header-anchor" href="#_17-3-4-complete-program-and-analysis" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;17.3.4 Complete Program and Analysis&quot;">​</a></h3><ol><li><p>Upon power-on, initialize the variable <code>speed</code> to 0. The fan remains stopped initially.</p></li><li><p>When the left button is short-pressed, if <code>speed</code> is less than 100, increase <code>speed</code> by 10 and update the fan speed on port A.</p></li><li><p>When the right button is short-pressed, if <code>speed</code> is greater than 0, decrease <code>speed</code> by 10 and update the fan speed on port A.</p></li></ol><img loading="lazy" height="605" width="398" src="' + _imports_3 + '" class="common_img" style="width:500px;"><div class="note custom-block github-alert"><p class="custom-block-title">NOTE</p><p></p><p><strong>The source files are available for download under <a href="https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/1fLfLXEVjSMZdojOq7C44xJqZIBm4MDem?usp=sharing" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">Program Files/ 17 Fan Module.sb3</a>.</strong></p></div><h3 id="_17-3-5-program-upload" tabindex="-1">17.3.5 Program Upload <a class="header-anchor" href="#_17-3-5-program-upload" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;17.3.5 Program Upload&quot;">​</a></h3><ul><li>Click <strong>Connect device</strong>, select the serial port, then click the upload button. Wait for the upload success notification to complete the program transfer.</li></ul><img loading="lazy" height="360" width="640" src="' + _imports_4 + '" class="common_img" style="width:800px;"><h3 id="_17-3-6-program-outcome" tabindex="-1">17.3.6 Program Outcome <a class="header-anchor" href="#_17-3-6-program-outcome" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;17.3.6 Program Outcome&quot;">​</a></h3><p>After uploading the program, the fan remains stationary at startup. Short-pressing the left button ramps up the fan speed in increments of 10 up to a maximum of 100. Short-pressing the right button lowers the speed step by step until it reaches 0, bringing the fan blades to a complete stop.</p>', 25)
